---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import PageIntro from "@/components/PageIntro.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config";
import { formatDate, isoDate } from "@/utils/content";
import { WEBSITE_ID, breadcrumbNode } from "@/utils/schema";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "Privacy", href: "/privacy" },
];
/** Change this date whenever the policy text changes. */
const updated = new Date("2026-10-28");
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What urielpapa.com collects and why: Google Analytics, the contact form, the Buttondown newsletter, Vercel hosting, and YouTube, X and Threads embeds. No ads, no data sold."
  modifiedTime={updated}
  schema={[breadcrumbNode(crumbs)]}
  webPage={{ about: { "@id": WEBSITE_ID } }}
>
  <div class="app-layout max-w-read pt-8">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
    <PageIntro
      title="Privacy policy"
      intro="What this site collects, which services handle it, and how to ask me to delete it."
    >
      <p class="meta mt-3">
        Last updated: <time datetime={isoDate(updated)}
          >{formatDate(updated, "D MMMM YYYY")}</time
        >
      </p>
    </PageIntro>
    <div class="app-prose">
      <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>
      <p>
        There are no ads on this site. I don't sell your data or share it for
        marketing. Everything that leaves your browser is listed below.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        I use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages people read. It loads only
        after you scroll, tap or press a key, or after 4 seconds. It records
        page views and a few events, such as newsletter signups, contact form
        submissions and clicks on some links. Ad storage and ad personalisation
        are always off. In the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, analytics cookies
        are off by default, so Google receives only cookieless measurements.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        When you send the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, your name, email
        address, topic and message go to Resend, an email service, which
        delivers them to my inbox. I use them only to reply to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        To stop spam, the form has a hidden field that only bots fill in, and
        the server briefly keeps IP addresses in memory to limit how many
        messages can be sent in a short time. When Cloudflare Turnstile is
        switched on, it runs a spam check in the form and your IP address is
        sent to Cloudflare to verify it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="newsletter">The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        Newsletter signups go to Buttondown. I send it your email address, your
        IP address, the page you signed up from and a short tag saying which
        signup box you used. Buttondown then emails you a confirmation link, and
        you are only subscribed after you click it. You can unsubscribe at any
        time. The same Turnstile spam check applies when it is switched on.
      </p>

      <h2 id="hosting">Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel keeps server
        logs of requests, which include IP addresses and browser details.
      </p>

      <h2 id="youtube">YouTube videos</h2>
      <p>
        Some posts include a YouTube video. Until you press play, only the
        thumbnail image loads, from YouTube's image server (i.ytimg.com). When
        you press play, the player loads from youtube-nocookie.com, YouTube's
        privacy-enhanced mode. Without JavaScript, the link opens the video on
        YouTube itself.
      </p>

      <h2 id="social-posts">X and Threads posts</h2>
      <p>
        Some news posts quote a post from X or Threads. At first you see a card
        with the post's text, served by this site, and nothing loads from X or
        Threads. If you press "Show the post on X" or "Show the post on
        Threads", the platform's own embed loads from X (platform.twitter.com)
        or Threads (threads.net), and that company may set cookies or log your
        visit under its own privacy policy. X's embed is asked not to track you
        ("Do Not Track"). The link under each card opens the post on the
        platform instead.
      </p>

      <h2 id="badge">The footer badge</h2>
      <p>
        The footer shows a badge image loaded from websitelaunches.com, so that
        site receives a normal image request from your browser.
      </p>

      <h2 id="browser">What stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        If you pick a light or dark theme, that choice is saved in your
        browser's local storage. It is never sent to me.
      </p>

      <h2 id="delete">Asking me to delete your data</h2>
      <p>
        To ask what I hold about you, or to have it deleted, write to me through
        the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or email <a
          href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a
        >. I will delete your messages and remove your address from the
        newsletter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
